WEBVTT

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:16.730
Got it!

00:00:18.290 --> 00:00:22.720
The Nivkh put seal fat on everything.

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:25.580
It's like soy sauce is to the Japanese.

00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:28.500
It's an important food source 
at this time of year.

00:00:31.690 --> 00:00:32.900
A reindeer.

00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:34.680
Did it come from the other side?

00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:40.180
It may have fled from the continent 
'cause something was chasing it, too.

00:01:05.370 --> 00:01:11.860
<b>Golden Kamuy</b>

00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:28.640
<b>Ako Prison</b>

00:02:30.790 --> 00:02:36.650
<b>Episode Thirty-Four
Catching Up to the Wolf</b>

00:02:40.380 --> 00:02:44.020
Use a bit of dirty snow to hide the holes.

00:02:44.020 --> 00:02:45.560
Don't put in too much,

00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:48.140
or we won't be able to get 
the explosives in later.

00:02:55.410 --> 00:02:56.550
Just like we thought.

00:02:56.550 --> 00:02:58.110
The lighthouse was empty.

00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:00.640
We got our explosives.

00:03:07.240 --> 00:03:10.440
The front is heavily guarded, so we'll go

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:13.650
around to the rear, the one 
facing the Strait of Tartary.

00:03:13.650 --> 00:03:15.170
We'll destroy these four spots at once.

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:20.130
And that's the signal to Sofia 
and her friends to flee.

00:03:20.130 --> 00:03:20.960
Yup.

00:03:20.960 --> 00:03:23.890
I told her to do it tomorrow at sunrise.

00:03:24.890 --> 00:03:26.670
We're ready.

00:03:26.670 --> 00:03:28.930
It's time, Asirpa.

00:03:29.350 --> 00:03:33.440
When you meet her, 
you'll remember something, I'm sure.

00:03:33.970 --> 00:03:36.180
I can't wait for that to happen.

00:04:17.230 --> 00:04:18.950
What's wrong, Shiraishi?

00:04:18.950 --> 00:04:20.710
Why didn't it blow?

00:04:20.710 --> 00:04:23.240
I set it up, but it didn't explode!

00:04:23.240 --> 00:04:24.980
Neither did mine!

00:04:26.350 --> 00:04:27.280
Shit!

00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:29.870
I guess it wasn't stored properly!

00:04:31.950 --> 00:04:33.400
Something exploded.

00:04:34.970 --> 00:04:36.210
That's Ako Prison.

00:04:38.020 --> 00:04:39.630
Don't go outside!

00:04:39.630 --> 00:04:41.300
Nobody move!

00:04:46.700 --> 00:04:48.260
Khorosho!

00:04:58.710 --> 00:05:00.420
Where's the hole?

00:05:00.670 --> 00:05:03.210
This wasn't the deal!

00:05:04.050 --> 00:05:05.280
There!

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:06.910
This way, everyone!

00:05:26.490 --> 00:05:27.600
That's strange.

00:05:31.720 --> 00:05:33.420
Nobody's coming out.

00:05:39.540 --> 00:05:41.650
What the hell is a tiger doing here?

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:46.070
That's not the right yulbars!

00:05:46.890 --> 00:05:50.420
<i>Yulbars means "tiger" in the Tatar language.</i>

00:05:51.840 --> 00:05:55.170
<i>The Siberian Tiger is the 
largest of all tigers,</i>

00:05:55.170 --> 00:05:58.150
<i>attacking and eating even 
bears and crocodiles.</i>

00:05:58.670 --> 00:06:05.530
<i>Sometimes it will cross the strait following
 prey, going far outside of its territory!</i>

00:06:10.530 --> 00:06:14.970
Do something about this tiger!
 We can't escape!

00:06:20.250 --> 00:06:23.860
We'll draw it away! Leave by that hole!

00:06:25.960 --> 00:06:31.760
Who do you think I am? No good 
leader leaves before her men.

00:06:31.760 --> 00:06:35.600
That's our Sofia!

00:06:52.930 --> 00:06:54.390
Shoot! Now!

00:06:54.390 --> 00:06:55.370
Don't.

00:06:57.950 --> 00:07:04.420
The Nanai say that tigers are gods, 
and killing them is bad luck.

00:07:09.160 --> 00:07:10.030
Okay!

00:07:11.930 --> 00:07:14.180
Another hole in the wall!

00:07:14.180 --> 00:07:15.970
Hurry, everyone!

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:26.320
That outfit...

00:07:27.180 --> 00:07:28.680
A Karafuto Ainu?

00:07:29.420 --> 00:07:31.880
Karafuto Ainu? No.

00:07:33.940 --> 00:07:36.080
Wilk showed me...

00:07:36.640 --> 00:07:39.500
He wore tetarape when he young.

00:07:42.230 --> 00:07:43.430
Those eyes.

00:07:43.980 --> 00:07:45.800
Wilk's eyes.

00:07:48.040 --> 00:07:49.220
Are you Sofia?

00:07:51.430 --> 00:07:52.780
Asirpa...

00:07:54.560 --> 00:07:56.660
This wasn't what I imagined.

00:07:57.100 --> 00:07:58.140
Sofia!

00:08:02.220 --> 00:08:04.690
You've grown into a lovely woman!

00:08:07.360 --> 00:08:08.970
Yulbars!

00:08:14.650 --> 00:08:17.280
What you did to Wilk...

00:08:21.410 --> 00:08:23.080
Let's go!

00:08:27.920 --> 00:08:28.710
This way!

00:08:33.470 --> 00:08:34.420
There!

00:08:34.420 --> 00:08:37.200
Wait, those are Nivkh fishermen!

00:08:41.570 --> 00:08:46.520
I only see Nivkh. 
Follow the ones who went to town!

00:08:56.030 --> 00:08:57.970
It worked!

00:08:58.210 --> 00:09:00.070
Nobody's following us.

00:09:00.070 --> 00:09:03.180
We were right to set the 
time of the escape for dawn,

00:09:03.180 --> 00:09:04.310
when there are lots of fishermen out.

00:09:12.660 --> 00:09:15.110
I want you to tell me about my father.

00:09:15.110 --> 00:09:17.530
Tell me things only you know.

00:09:19.840 --> 00:09:23.290
She wants to know about Wilk.

00:09:27.980 --> 00:09:31.820
He was pure and beautiful.

00:09:35.320 --> 00:09:39.800
I grew up in a fancy house, 
wearing expensive clothes.

00:09:40.950 --> 00:09:43.640
I was a rich girl who only knew the cities.

00:09:47.140 --> 00:09:50.060
I met them as part of the 
revolutionary movement.

00:09:52.040 --> 00:09:55.480
They taught me of many things I didn't know.

00:09:57.140 --> 00:09:59.050
Salt-preserved lingonberries...

00:09:59.820 --> 00:10:02.080
Karafuto Ainu dog sleds...

00:10:02.360 --> 00:10:04.750
Hohchiri, tied to the bangs...

00:10:05.380 --> 00:10:07.660
The bone fortunetelling of the Uilta...

00:10:08.430 --> 00:10:11.700
The clothes of the Nivkh,
made from seal and fish skins...

00:10:12.630 --> 00:10:16.550
The lives of the ethnic minorities 
who lived in the Far East...

00:10:20.550 --> 00:10:23.020
Our unique languages...

00:10:23.670 --> 00:10:25.400
The gods we believe in...

00:10:34.450 --> 00:10:37.840
If we don't fight to protect them,
they'll all disappear.

00:10:39.040 --> 00:10:43.810
The new generation of children will 
forget their language and their gods.

00:10:53.470 --> 00:10:58.040
Why did the natives of the 
Americas lose to the white man?

00:10:58.660 --> 00:11:02.680
Because all the tribes were 
at war with one another.

00:11:03.670 --> 00:11:05.520
I'm told that in Japan's Hokkaido,

00:11:05.520 --> 00:11:10.380
there are a people with traditions 
very similar to the Karafuto Ainu.

00:11:15.230 --> 00:11:20.520
Each of them are small in number, 
but if we all cooperate...

00:11:21.210 --> 00:11:22.570
Cooperate?

00:11:23.040 --> 00:11:26.080
We need to make a federation
 of far eastern states,

00:11:26.510 --> 00:11:29.350
including Karafuto and Hokkaido.

00:11:33.790 --> 00:11:35.260
That's a big deal.

00:11:42.220 --> 00:11:45.430
Kiroranke blew the wall and 
let the prisoners escape.

00:11:45.910 --> 00:11:48.680
We were a little late, but they're close.

00:11:50.090 --> 00:11:51.320
Well, Ryuu?

00:11:54.250 --> 00:11:55.380
That way?

00:11:55.380 --> 00:11:56.690
Did you find the scent?

00:11:57.150 --> 00:12:01.780
Don't tell me they ran across the ice floes.

00:12:05.920 --> 00:12:09.410
If Ryuu says it's the way, I believe it.

00:12:11.300 --> 00:12:12.460
What's wrong, you two?

00:12:14.540 --> 00:12:15.670
A tiger?!

00:12:27.340 --> 00:12:29.640
<i>One of those gunshots was long,</i>

00:12:29.640 --> 00:12:33.900
<i>like you'd hear from a gun 
that used old black gunpowder.</i>

00:12:35.870 --> 00:12:36.930
<i>No, it can't be.</i>

00:12:42.940 --> 00:12:45.950
<b>Golden Kamuy</b>

00:12:56.300 --> 00:12:58.150
Shiraishi, where are you going?

00:12:58.150 --> 00:12:59.710
Go on without me.

00:13:01.430 --> 00:13:03.810
I need to piss.

00:13:03.810 --> 00:13:07.550
It's hard to get my willie 
out with all these layers.

00:13:10.610 --> 00:13:12.180
That was close.

00:13:14.860 --> 00:13:16.190
It's getting bigger!

00:13:16.190 --> 00:13:19.140
The ice floes move around with the current!

00:13:19.140 --> 00:13:21.230
Don't fall in the ocean!

00:13:21.230 --> 00:13:22.630
What do I do?

00:13:22.630 --> 00:13:24.980
I can't get back!

00:13:24.980 --> 00:13:28.450
Just head west! We'll meet there!

00:13:29.280 --> 00:13:33.080
I don't think I can get there this way.

00:13:33.470 --> 00:13:35.690
I'll have better luck heading back!

00:13:35.690 --> 00:13:38.210
I'll hurry and catch up, so wait for me!

00:13:38.600 --> 00:13:40.360
Be careful, Shiraishi!

00:13:40.360 --> 00:13:42.460
If you fall in while 
you're alone, you're dead!

00:13:42.710 --> 00:13:47.160
Got it? Don't fall! Don't fall!

00:13:52.250 --> 00:13:56.100
It's not easy to get over this 
rough terrain with a sled!

00:13:56.100 --> 00:13:58.330
And the weather's getting bad, too.

00:13:58.330 --> 00:14:00.190
It may be dangerous to follow them.

00:14:00.190 --> 00:14:02.500
You saw that explosion!

00:14:02.500 --> 00:14:04.500
They're close!

00:14:08.200 --> 00:14:10.390
Ryuu's going crazy, too!

00:14:12.390 --> 00:14:13.550
We can find them if we go now!

00:14:13.550 --> 00:14:15.530
Wait, Sugimoto!

00:14:18.570 --> 00:14:20.290
Look, Asirpa.

00:14:24.920 --> 00:14:26.030
Wolves.

00:14:26.650 --> 00:14:28.150
Will they come this way?

00:14:28.150 --> 00:14:29.130
I doubt it.

00:14:29.800 --> 00:14:32.670
Were they the ones after that reindeer?

00:14:33.490 --> 00:14:35.620
Wilk liked wolves.

00:14:35.620 --> 00:14:39.020
He said they were pure and beautiful.

00:14:45.130 --> 00:14:47.780
Wolves are beautiful.

00:14:48.470 --> 00:14:51.210
They lead strong lives, with nothing wasted.

00:14:51.210 --> 00:14:53.120
That's what makes them beautiful.

00:14:54.160 --> 00:14:57.290
Beauty and strength are the same.

00:14:57.640 --> 00:15:01.700
Here's a story about Wilk for you...

00:15:05.330 --> 00:15:11.050
One night, we were being chased by the 
secret police, and fled into the forest.

00:15:12.200 --> 00:15:15.970
One of us was badly wounded 
and couldn't move at all.

00:15:18.280 --> 00:15:21.000
He passed out,

00:15:21.000 --> 00:15:23.440
and stopped us from moving.

00:15:27.560 --> 00:15:32.040
When our pursuers were getting close and 
his moans threatened to alert them...

00:15:40.970 --> 00:15:45.060
He wasn't going to survive either way,

00:15:45.610 --> 00:15:49.400
and we ended up barely being missed.

00:15:50.670 --> 00:15:52.210
If it had been me,

00:15:52.210 --> 00:15:57.690
I would've hesitated and fretted before 
finally reaching the same conclusion, maybe.

00:15:59.740 --> 00:16:04.570
But Wilk was someone who could reach that 
answer in the minimum distance needed.

00:16:09.190 --> 00:16:12.720
I trusted him from the bottom of my heart.

00:16:13.390 --> 00:16:14.730
And loved him.

00:16:20.070 --> 00:16:21.740
We're shooting the baby bear, too?

00:16:22.690 --> 00:16:24.660
We can't take it to the kotan?

00:16:26.380 --> 00:16:29.380
It's too big to raise.

00:16:30.470 --> 00:16:32.850
Do you think it's cruel, Asirpa?

00:16:35.050 --> 00:16:37.690
That parent and child will 
become blood and meat,

00:16:37.690 --> 00:16:40.130
and sustain our lives.

00:16:40.810 --> 00:16:43.020
Even a baby bear is a 
precious source of food.

00:16:43.460 --> 00:16:47.270
If we hesitate because it's cruel, we starve.

00:16:48.360 --> 00:16:52.240
Pity and kindness that is 
wrong can become weakness.

00:16:54.680 --> 00:16:57.420
<i>The weak lose, and are eaten.</i>

00:17:02.520 --> 00:17:06.440
Do you know where Wilk's name came from?

00:17:07.390 --> 00:17:09.870
Where his name came from?

00:17:09.870 --> 00:17:12.120
No, I don't.

00:17:13.640 --> 00:17:15.480
Do you know, Asirpa?

00:17:17.010 --> 00:17:20.190
I think he told me one time.

00:17:21.330 --> 00:17:22.600
What was it?

00:17:26.430 --> 00:17:31.000
There was one big thing that 
happened that made him who he was.

00:17:32.220 --> 00:17:35.740
Before his name was Wilk,

00:17:36.460 --> 00:17:40.330
he found a weakened wolf near the kotan.

00:17:42.850 --> 00:17:46.870
He came to see it every day.

00:17:50.500 --> 00:17:54.790
And eventually, it began to howl.

00:17:58.140 --> 00:18:00.520
And howls answered it.

00:18:02.230 --> 00:18:05.140
Wilk understood that he wanted 
to go back to his pack,

00:18:05.810 --> 00:18:11.400
and had become a lone wolf because 
he had an illness or some other defect.

00:18:13.590 --> 00:18:16.780
The pack came for him.

00:18:18.910 --> 00:18:22.150
But the pack killed him.

00:18:24.200 --> 00:18:28.100
They decided there was no 
room for him in the pack.

00:18:29.320 --> 00:18:33.950
If a single wolf slows them down, 
it's a threat to the whole pack.

00:18:37.010 --> 00:18:38.890
Wolves are logical and rational.

00:18:39.460 --> 00:18:44.760
Any extra kindness in them has been 
scraped away to ensure they survive.

00:18:46.330 --> 00:18:49.350
A functional beauty, with nothing wasted.

00:18:49.350 --> 00:18:52.040
That's what he felt in 
the way the wolves lived.

00:18:57.680 --> 00:18:59.970
He wanted to be a creature like that.

00:18:59.970 --> 00:19:04.050
So he stripped the corpse of its 
pelt and ran around wearing it.

00:19:05.880 --> 00:19:09.200
His Polish father looked at him,

00:19:10.140 --> 00:19:12.710
and decided his name then.

00:19:14.720 --> 00:19:15.990
"Wilk."

00:19:17.530 --> 00:19:21.680
Wilk means "wolf" in Polish.

00:19:33.150 --> 00:19:35.260
Tell me about Mommy.

00:19:35.830 --> 00:19:37.020
Again?

00:19:37.660 --> 00:19:41.160
She was a beautiful woman, just like you.

00:19:42.220 --> 00:19:43.960
We met in Otaru.

00:19:44.690 --> 00:19:48.040
She taught me all the things I didn't know.

00:19:49.900 --> 00:19:53.970
The language of the Hokkaido Ainu,
 and their beliefs.

00:19:56.100 --> 00:19:59.750
Never forget what I'm about to tell you.

00:20:01.500 --> 00:20:08.660
I once told your mom how 
I got the name Wilk...

00:20:09.350 --> 00:20:13.950
And then she gave me a name in Ainu.

00:20:16.550 --> 00:20:18.670
Horkew Oskoni.

00:20:20.050 --> 00:20:21.940
Horkew Oskoni?

00:20:24.160 --> 00:20:26.830
It means "catching up to the wolf."

00:20:29.100 --> 00:20:31.240
Because I wanted to be a wolf.

00:20:32.660 --> 00:20:38.260
The only ones who know this name are myself, 
and your mother, who gave it to me.

00:20:39.440 --> 00:20:41.560
You mustn't tell it to anyone.

00:20:50.730 --> 00:20:52.000
Hey, Sugimoto.

00:20:52.000 --> 00:20:53.520
How do you read this?

00:20:53.850 --> 00:20:54.940
"U."

00:20:54.940 --> 00:20:56.680
Like in "ukai," to go around.

00:21:20.630 --> 00:21:22.680
Shit! Shit!

00:21:29.180 --> 00:21:32.970
Dick talisman... protect me!

00:21:36.430 --> 00:21:38.550
Behold the power of dick.

00:21:41.850 --> 00:21:43.130
No way!

00:21:57.710 --> 00:21:59.980
Hey, Shiraishi Yoshitake.

00:22:01.020 --> 00:22:02.200
We meet again.

00:23:34.930 --> 00:23:40.250
<b>Next Time
Sin and Impurity</b>

00:23:36.000 --> 00:23:39.500
Next time: "Sin and Impurity."
